  <h2>Common questions</h2>
  <h3>Can I reorder messages?</h3>
  <p>
    There's no drag-and-drop yet. Because every menu item inserts <em>below</em> the message you
    opened it on, the practical approach is to add the new message in the right place to begin
    with, or delete and re-add. For a big reshuffle it's faster to edit the script and generate
    again.
  </p>
  <h3>Does editing the preview overwrite my script?</h3>
  <p>
    No — they're independent. The script is a starting point; once generated, the preview is the
    source of truth. Hitting <strong>Generate Chat</strong> again rebuilds the conversation from
    the script, so do your script edits first and your preview edits second.
  </p>
  <h3>Can I edit on my phone?</h3>
  <p>
    Yes. The editor works on mobile — the script and preview become tabs you switch between.
    Tap-to-edit works the same as click-to-edit, and the hover buttons appear on tap.
  </p>
  <h3>Do edits show up in the exported video?</h3>
  <p>
    Everything you see in the preview is what gets exported, in both PNG and MP4 — including
    reactions, voice notes, call logs and your edited timestamps.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ethics">Use it responsibly</h2>
  <p>
    These tools are for <strong>clearly fictional</strong> content: stories, skits, memes,
    product demos, presentations and teaching examples. Don't use them to impersonate real
    people, fabricate evidence, or mislead anyone — that can be illegal, and it's why the export
    asks you to confirm your chat is fictional. If you're publishing somewhere it could be taken
    for a real conversation, label it as a mockup.
  </p>

